{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 9: Temperature Control",
  "description": "See how temperature affects randomness in generation!\n\nTEMPERATURE IS THE CREATIVITY DIAL:\n- Low (0.1): Almost deterministic, always picks most likely\n- Medium (1.0): Balanced, natural randomness\n- High (2.0): Very random, surprising choices\n\nTHE MATH:\n1. Logits / temperature\n2. Softmax to probabilities\n3. Sample from distribution\n\nLow temp -> peaked distribution -> same token every time\nHigh temp -> flat distribution -> random tokens\n\nTRY THIS:\n1. Set temperature to 0.1 - run many times, notice same output\n2. Set temperature to 2.0 - run many times, notice variety\n3. Find YOUR sweet spot for creativity vs coherence\n\nThis is why Claude has a temperature setting!",
