    {
      "id": "comment-0723d318-3852-498f-8a85-f2d25f326df2",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "name": "Welcome",
      "position": [
        50,
        50
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": "# Temperature - Controlling Randomness\n\nTemperature controls how \"creative\" vs \"focused\" outputs are.\n\n## To Do and Notice\n\n1. **Low temperature (0.1)**: Very deterministic, picks top choice\n2. **Medium (1.0)**: Balanced, natural distribution\n3. **High (2.0+)**: More random, creative, chaotic\n\n## The Math\n\n```\nprobs = softmax(logits / temperature)\n```\n\nDividing by temperature before softmax changes the distribution shape.\n\n## In Practice\n\n- Code generation: Low temp (0.2-0.4)\n- Creative writing: Higher temp (0.7-1.0)\n- Brainstorming: Even higher (1.2+)\n\n**Challenge**: Find the \"sweet spot\" for different tasks.",
        "width": 450,
        "show_on_start": true
      },
      "inputs": {},
      "outputs": {},
      "weights": {},
      "collapsed": false,
      "color": "#5c4a3d",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Tutorial introduction"
    }
